Hey Chris --

Great work on adding NPC behavior. Makes NH a more interesting game!

There are a couple of things that I've been thinking about, but not directly
related to the priest, but rather to the temple.

Having a degree in Religious Studies, I was exposed to a lot of different
theories on what religion and 'sacred' is. Mircea Eliade argued that
'sacred' simply means 'set apart', 'seperate', or 'other'. In creating
sacred spaces, such as temples, people around the world use various devices
to set the sacred space apart from regular space. One of these techniques
are walls, which demarcate the sacred space.

Thus, it always confused me when a dwarve busted through the walls of a
temple and
1. Did not get his ass fried and
2. The priest still hung around the desecrated temple.

Now I know that wall-building has been proposed before and will probably not
be implented. But I was thinking that a temple area that has either missing
wall sections or has a busted door should lose its sacrality. The priest
could then re-dedicate the temple using wizard lock (if they know it), or
abandon it if the walls have been broken. Or, perhaps if there is a suitable
room on the same level, they could move the altar, and make a new temple.

